PowOS: Xwayland hang fix - miSyncTriggerFence walks a fence's triggers once (xserver master).

Against lotfibennour/andromarchy @ 220754d390f743aa5a8227e689402de1a6eb0281: a fifth patch for the Xwayland that
build-inside.sh compiles (24.1.13 + lfdevs's KGSL patches). The hang is described in the patch header.

--- a/patches/xwayland/0005-misync-trigger-fence-single-pass.patch	1970-01-01 01:00:00
+++ b/patches/xwayland/0005-misync-trigger-fence-single-pass.patch	2026-10-16 17:34:20
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+From: PowOS
+Subject: misync: run a fence's triggers once (xserver master), not until none fires
+
+24.1's miSyncTriggerFence restarts its trigger walk until no trigger fires.
+Present's wait-fence trigger counts as fired while its callback is set, and the
+callback stays set when xwl_present_re_execute requeues the request for a later
+MSC (KGSL surfaceless: no flips, frame callbacks held back), so it loops
+forever inside ProcSyncDispatch: Xwayland spins a core and stops serving
+clients. Seen with Steam's web UI and Proton games (DXVK) on Adreno/KGSL.
+
+xserver master walks the list once, keeping the next entry before firing.
+---
+ miext/sync/misync.c | 18 ++++++------------
+ 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/miext/sync/misync.c b/miext/sync/misync.c
+--- a/miext/sync/misync.c
++++ b/miext/sync/misync.c
+@@ -135,22 +135,16 @@
+ void
+ miSyncTriggerFence(SyncFence * pFence)
+ {
+-    SyncTriggerList *ptl;
+-    Bool triggered;
++    SyncTriggerList *ptl, *pNext;
+ 
+     pFence->funcs.SetTriggered(pFence);
+ 
+     /* run through triggers to see if any fired */
+-    do {
+-        triggered = FALSE;
+-        for (ptl = pFence->sync.pTriglist; ptl; ptl = ptl->next) {
+-            if ((*ptl->pTrigger->CheckTrigger) (ptl->pTrigger, 0)) {
+-                (*ptl->pTrigger->TriggerFired) (ptl->pTrigger);
+-                triggered = TRUE;
+-                break;
+-            }
+-        }
+-    } while (triggered);
++    for (ptl = pFence->sync.pTriglist; ptl; ptl = pNext) {
++        pNext = ptl->next;
++        if ((*ptl->pTrigger->CheckTrigger) (ptl->pTrigger, 0))
++            (*ptl->pTrigger->TriggerFired) (ptl->pTrigger);
++    }
+ }
+ 
+ SyncScreenFuncsPtr
